# Cs+/O+ Multi-fluid MHD for Cesium Cloud

## Overview

This directory contains parameter files for multi-fluid Cs+/O+ MHD simulations
of ionospheric cesium cloud releases. Unlike the single-fluid multi-species
approach, this uses true multifluid physics with separate velocities for each
ion species, enabling proper parallel vs perpendicular conductivity anisotropy.

## Build Instructions

### 1. Configure BATSRUS

```bash
cd BATSRUS
Config.pl -e=MhdCsOpMulti -u=CsCloudMulti -g=16,16,1
```

Where:
- `-e=MhdCsOpMulti`: Two-fluid Cs+/O+ equation module (ModEquationMhdCsOpMulti.f90)
- `-u=CsCloudMulti`: Cesium cloud user module (ModUserCsCloudMulti.f90)
- `-g=16,16,1`: 2D grid (adjust as needed)

### 2. Compile

```bash
make BATSRUS
```

### 3. Run Night Test

```bash
cd run
cp ../Param/CSMULTI/PARAM.in .
mpirun -np 4 ./BATSRUS.exe
```

## Parameter Files

- `PARAM.in`: Night 10-minute smoke test (UseDayPhoto=F)
  - 2D Cartesian: x (horizontal perp), y (|| B)
  - Domain: 100 km x 100 km
  - B = 40 uT along +y (F-region ~200 km)
  - Cloud: R0=1km at (25km, 0), Epsilon0=1e-3 seed
  - Run time: 600 s (10 min)

## Physics Parameters

Key collision coefficients (FP defaults from first-principles @ 200 km):
- `NuCsO_coef = 6.2e-10 cm^3/s`: Cs+-O collision (Banks/Zhang F-region)
- `NuOpCs_coef = 1.2e-11 cm^3/s`: O+-Cs+ inter-fluid momentum exchange
- `NuPh = 6.5e-4 /s`: Daytime photoionization (set to 0 for night)
- `Epsilon0 = 1e-3`: Non-equilibrium ionization seed (night thermal)

## Multi-fluid vs Multi-species

| Feature | Multi-species (old) | Multi-fluid (new) |
|---------|---------------------|-------------------|
| Velocities | Shared u | Separate u_Cs, u_O |
| IsMhd | .true. | .false. |
| Anisotropy | sigma_||/sigma_perp ~ 1 | sigma_|| > sigma_perp |
| Variables | Rho, RhoCsp, RhoOp, RhoU, B, p | CspRho, CspRhoU, CspP, OpRho, OpRhoU, OpP, B |

## Known Limitations

- This PR provides equation stack + templates; anisotropy demonstration requires
  actual simulation runs and analysis
- Oxidation, attachment, mutual neutralization switches default OFF
- Stratified atmosphere (#CSSTRAT) optional; default uses uniform background

## References

- Glocer et al. multi-ion fluid formulation in BATSRUS
- Banks/Zhang F-region collision frequencies
- Schunk & Nagy ionosphere-thermosphere coupling
- CSCLOUD data pack v0.2 (first-principles 200 km parameters)

## Contact

For cesium cloud physics questions, refer to CSCLOUD documentation.
For BATSRUS multi-ion implementation, see ModMultiFluid.f90 and related modules.
